Z||000017||Pontiaddict||12-02-2001||10:04 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>Cute pics, but the article is ignorant and baseless...<P>I got news for you guys...when most people see a Fiero, they don't think "there's a domestic similar to an old Camaro SS" they think "there's a ricer!". <P>In the few miles I have on mine, I've already experienced the full ignorance of a Monte Carlo SS (the old "real" ones). "Nice Jap crap!"<P>Oh well...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually it was right on target.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>From Car Craft Magazine<B><BR>Now, before you get all riled at us, know that we are not so nieve as to think that we're invincible to evert import car. We've been mopped up by enough modded Supras and RX-7's to know and respect their reputations on the street and at the track. Anyone driving a serious street machine is a friend of ours. But the posers, wannabes anjokers who impersonate hot rodders and perpetuate our allready bad reputation in the popular media, listen up! We're calling you out. We're calling out the guy who shows up at the Friday night test and tune, talks smack but never runs his own car, and tears around the parking lot smoking the tires and endangering our saftey. We're calling out the convoys of idiots who weave in and out of traffic on crowded freeways. We're calling out the sore loser that hurls a pop can at a car whose driver is too smart to risk his life racing on the street.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
